\setinaudiodev sets the audio input device used by
Python (pyo).
It takes one argument, the ID of the device, as printed
by \listaudiodev:

\listaudiodev
\setinaudiodev 1

If the ID is negative or not in the list, you will get
an error.
Like all audio settings, it must be called before \python
is called for the first time, otherwise it has no effect.

To set the output device, use \setoutaudiodev, and to set
both at once, use \setaudiodev.
